<%# == One repeated description, opened
        The rung BELOW the panel above, whose rows dead-ended.
        That ranking says a description is carried by eight examples costing ninety seconds between
        them and names the files they ran in; until this panel there was no way whatever to learn
        WHICH eight, what each cost, where each sits or how each ended — `repeated_descriptions_in`
        is an aggregate out of which no member row escapes.

        And NOT reachable through the `?spec_file=` panel above, which is the obvious substitute and
        does not work: that panel lists every example of a file, capped at fifty and ranked by
        duration, so a reader following a two-file group through it gets two lists of up to fifty
        unrelated rows — and this group's own members need not be among the fifty either list shows.
        The narrowing this needs is by DESCRIPTION.

        The claim boundary is INHERITED WHOLE from the panel above and nothing here widens it. A
        shared description is equally a table-driven loop, a shared example group, or the same test
        written twice, and nothing on this page decides which — so nothing below uses the word
        "duplicate", and the rows carry where, when, how long and how it ended, and no verdict. What
        the rows add is what the reader DECIDES from: three consecutive line numbers in one file read
        as a loop, one definition site included by four files reads as a shared example group, and
        the same sentence at three unrelated sites reads as neither.

        Rendered only when a description was ASKED for, and the read is taken only then: a page
        nobody asked a description of costs exactly what it cost before this existed.

        An EQUALITY predicate on `name`, riding `index_spec_observations_on_test_run_id` — one query
        bounded by the size of one RUN. See `SpecObservation.with_description`, where a plain `DESC`
        would head a list captioned "slowest first" with the examples that never ran.

        Same visibility rule and same gate as the panels above: read-only suite telemetry on
        `current_repository(:view)`, outside `manage_keys`, and nothing here widens that. %>
<% if @repeated_description_examples %>
      <%= render UI::PanelComponent.new(title: "Examples under this description",
                                        id: "repeated-description-examples", class: "rc-drill") do |panel| %>
        <% panel.with_actions do %>
          <%# The way back OUT of THIS ask only (`repeated_description: nil`, explicit); every other ask
              rides through, so closing a description closes no file or area. %>
          <%= render UI::ButtonComponent.new(
                variant: :ghost, size: :sm,
                href: drill_down_path(@repository, repeated_description: nil, anchor: "repeated-descriptions")
              ) { "Close description" } %>
        <% end %>
        <% if @repeated_description_examples.recorded? %>
          <%= render UI::NoteComponent.new(summary: "How to read this", id: "repeated-description-examples-basis") do %>
            <span class="text-app-content-secondary"><%= @repeated_description_examples.name %></span>
            — <%= repeated_description_examples_scope_sentence(@repeated_description_examples) %>
            <%# With `?layer=` asked the group holds only that layer's examples — exactly the rows the
                clicked ranking row counted — so "the same fraction the row states" below stays true,
                and every figure here is that layer's. %>
            <% if @repeated_description_examples.layer? %>
              Only the examples that declared <code><%= @repeated_description_examples.layer %></code>
              as their layer in their own <code>@intent</code> (never inferred from the path) are
              counted here, which is the population the row in the panel above counts.
            <% end %>
            <% if @repeated_description_examples.complete? %>
              <% if @repeated_description_examples.truncated? %>
                Every one of the
                <%= number_with_delimiter(@repeated_description_examples.recorded_count) %> reported
                a duration, so the ranking these
                <%= number_with_delimiter(@repeated_description_examples.rows.size) %> were drawn
                from covers the whole of what this run recorded here — the cap is all that keeps the
                rest off this page.
              <% else %>
                Every one of them reported a duration, so the list covers the whole of what this run
                recorded here.
              <% end %>
            <% elsif @repeated_description_examples.any_timed? %>
              Durations here cover <%= @repeated_description_examples.coverage_label %> — the same
              fraction the row for this description states in the panel above.
              <% if @repeated_description_examples.untimed_omitted_count.zero? %>
                The other
                <%= number_with_delimiter(@repeated_description_examples.untimed_count) %> reported
                none and sit at the END of the list rather than at the head of it.
              <% elsif @repeated_description_examples.lists_untimed? %>
                The other
                <%= number_with_delimiter(@repeated_description_examples.untimed_count) %> reported
                none:
                <%= number_with_delimiter(@repeated_description_examples.shown_untimed_count) %> of
                those are at the END of this list rather than at the head of it, and the remaining
                <%= number_with_delimiter(@repeated_description_examples.untimed_omitted_count) %>
                are not on this page at all.
              <% else %>
                The other
                <%= number_with_delimiter(@repeated_description_examples.untimed_count) %> reported
                none, and the cap was reached before the list got to any of them — none are on this
                page at all.
              <% end %>
              An example that never ran has no duration to report, so a missing timing is a faithful
              record rather than a gap — and it is not a zero.
            <% end %>
            Each row names both the file that RAN it and the file and line where it is DEFINED. Those
            differ when a shared example group is included by more than one file, and rows sharing
            one definition site are one test run more than once rather than a description written
            more than once.
          <% end %>
          <%= render UI::TableComponent.new(
                columns: ["Ran in", "Defined at", "Layer", { label: "Duration", end: true }, "Outcome"],
                describedby: "repeated-description-examples-basis", sortable: true) do %>
            <% @repeated_description_examples.rows.each do |observation| %>
              <tr>
                <td class="font-mono text-xs [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">
                  <% if observation.spec_file_path.present? %>
                    <%= link_to observation.spec_file_path,
                                drill_down_path(@repository, spec_file: observation.spec_file_path, anchor: "slow"),
                                class: "rc-link", aria: { current: observation.spec_file_path == @spec_file_request ? "true" : nil } %>
                  <% else %><span class="text-app-content-secondary">not reported</span><% end %>
                </td>
                <td>
                  <%= link_to observation.location_label,
                              @repository.github_blob_url(observation.file_path, observation.line_number, @latest_test_run.commit_sha),
                              class: "rc-ext", target: "_blank", rel: "noopener noreferrer" %>
                  <%= render "repositories/authored_intent", observation: observation %>
                </td>
                <td><%= declared_layer_label(observation) %></td>
                <td class="num" data-sort="<%= observation.duration_seconds %>"><%= observation.duration_label %></td>
                <td><%= render UI::BadgeComponent.new(tone: observation.outcome_tone) { observation.outcome_label } %></td>
              </tr>
            <% end %>
          <% end %>
        <% else %>
          <%= render UI::EmptyStateComponent.new(
                title: "No examples under this description",
                description: "This run recorded no example described " \
                             "“#{@repeated_description_examples.name}”. It may have been renamed or " \
                             "reworded since, or never have run in this run at all — the " \
                             "“Descriptions this run recorded more than once” table lists the " \
                             "descriptions this run did record under more than one example."
              ) %>
        <% end %>
      <% end %>
    <% end %>
